      "message": "@guillaume.boutry@canonical.com While testing this E2E on a local deployment, I noticed that volume-dd-blocksize never reaches the rendered cinder.conf for the ceph backend. cinder-volume-ceph is the only driver charm that overrides get_backend_configuration() with a hardcoded dict, bypassing the generic configuration_class pipeline in ops-sunbeam, so the new option is silently dropped for ceph. The other drivers use the base implementation, so they should work fine.\n\nWe could fix it by passing the option through the ceph-specific context and backend dict, matching the existing backend-availability-zone pattern. This would bypass the ge\u003d512 pydantic check in ops-sunbeam, however, so for ceph an invalid value would be rejected by the snap\u0027s own validation rather than a clean blocked status.",
